  "kind": "pose",
  "note": "Feeding on a kill on the ground in front: the head plunges down and forward, bites, wrenches up and sideways with the whole neck, swallows, and plunges again. Two lunges a loop, the second from a little further round, so a run of loops reads as worrying a carcass rather than pecking one spot. The body leans into each plunge and the wings half-lift on the wrench, the way a bird of prey mantles over food; the feet stay planted throughout. Loops: the first and last keys are the same crouched, head-raised pause between mouthfuls.",
